 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a first-time home buyer tax credit in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"SC Housing no longer offers its tax credit certificate. The tax break an owner gets here is the 4 percent rate on the home you live in, which needs an application to the county assessor."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a homestead exemption for first-time buyers in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not for being a first-time buyer. In South Carolina the homestead exemption is for owners 65 or older who have lived in the state a year, or who are disabled or blind. It exempts the first $50,000 of the home's value."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there help if I earn more than SC Housing's limit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Palmetto Home Advantage, another SC Housing program, has an income limit of $140,000 in every county, counted on the buyers' own income, not the whole household. It is open to first-time and repeat buyers. Its help is forgiven after 10 years, and repaid in full on a sale, refinance or move before then."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the FHA loan limit in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"FHA's 2026 loan limit for a one-unit home in Horry County is about $541,000. That is well above HUD's own estimate of the area's middle sale price, $340,000."}}]}</script>
