wBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Seller-paid closing costs</strong><span class="t">on FHA and VA</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span><strong>$10,000 from SC Housing</strong><span class="t">under its income limit</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Your cash to buy in Myrtle Beach is the down payment plus the closing costs, and a first-time buyer can often bring less of each.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The down payment depends on your loan, and your lender gives you that figure with your pre-approval. Part of your cash as a first-time buyer is earnest money, the deposit you give with your offer, which in an ordinary sale is credited to you at closing.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A VA loan often needs no down payment. A USDA loan can cover the full price inside USDA's area, mostly around Conway, Loris, Aynor and Longs, for low- and moderate-income buyers. On an FHA loan the seller can pay your closing costs. SC Housing adds $10,000 for buyers under its income limit.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Homes in your budget, checked for you</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me homes in my budget</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#cash" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Cash</a></li><li><a href="#what-it-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What it buys</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where</a></li><li><a href="#condo-or-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Condo or house</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1