tyle="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Mostly inland. The most sold around Conway and Longs, then in Socastee, southwest of Myrtle Beach. In one of Conway's ZIP codes, about 7 in 10 houses and townhouses that sold went for under $300,000. In North Myrtle Beach it was about 1 in 12.</p><figure class="c3-ft-map" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:560px"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 430" role="img" aria-label="Map of Horry County with a dot for each house or townhouse that sold for under $300,000 in the past year. The dots crowd around Conway, Longs and Loris, along the roads between them, and in Socastee southwest of Myrtle Beach. Few are near the beach in North Myrtle Beach."><defs><clipPath id="c3-ft-frame"><rect width="440" height="430"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#c3-ft-frame)"><rect width="440" height="430" fill="#e9e3d8"/><path d="M288.7,337.4L289.1,337.1L296.8,331.4L301.1,328.6L304.0,326.7L308.7,323.2L312.5,321.0L323.2,315.7L328.8,313.3L333.6,311.2L336.6,309.9L341.8,308.1L343.4,307.7L348.3,305.3L355.7,302.8L364.7,300.1L376.6,298.2L389.1,295.6L398.0,290.0L400.0,289.6L399.9,289.4L390.8,279.4L387.8,276.0L383.8,271.6L380.2,267.7L378.9,266.4L377.7,265.1L377.2,264.6L376.1,263.4L372.6,259.8L372.4,259.6L372.1,259.3L370.7,257.8L369.3,256.4L369.1,256.2L367.0,254.0L366.7,253.7L366.5,253.5L366.3,253.3L365.7,252.7L365.6,252.6L365.2,252.2L364.8,251.7L364.1,251.0L362.3,249.1L360.0,246.8L359.3,246.1L356.8,243.5L355.6,242.3L352.5,239.1L346.6,233.1L341.5,227.9L339.9,226.2L339.5,225.7L338.3,224.6L335.1,221.3L329.9,216.0L322.7,208.7L313.8,199.5L309.0,194.6L301.5,187.0L299.3,184.7L293.1,178.3L291.6,176.9L290.7,176.0L290.1,175.4L287.6,172.8L285.0,170.2L283.2,168.3L276.3,161.3L271.6,156.5L270.6,155.5L268.7,153.6L266.0,150.8L263.4,148.2L262.6,147.4L261.3,146.0L258.1,142.7L256.3,141.0L255.1,139.7L254.2,138.8L253.2,137.7L252.9,137.5L251.3,135.9L250.8,135.3L247.0,131.5L241.8,126.2L239.8,124.1L235.7,119.9L234